{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_4773f2hjknu2cjy2glbuumm3sx33usbsx7azkrurxnlignedmvga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. The implementation is working correctly:\n\n- `test_default` - Default context (SHA-384, default salt length)\n- `test_deterministic` - Deterministic blinding (SHA-384, salt_len=0)\n- `test_custom_parameters` - Custom context (SHA-256, salt_len=48)\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n1. **State management via side-channel maps**: The Rust types `BRSAContext`, `BRSAPublicKey`, `BRSASecretKey` have placeholder fields (`Option<EVP_PKEY>` etc.) that are opaque enums and can't store real data, so I use thread-safe `HashMap`s keyed by struct address to maintain the actual OpenSSL `Rsa` objects and context state.\n\n2. **PSS padding/verification implemented in pure Rust**: Custom `pss_encode`/`pss_verify` and `mgf1` functions because the openssl crate's high-level API doesn't expose `RSA_padding_add_PKCS1_PSS_mgf1` directly with custom modulus operations needed for blinding.\n\n3. **Blinding logic**: Uses `BigNum` arithmetic from the `openssl` crate (`mod_mul`, `mod_exp`, `mod_inverse`, `gcd`, `rand_range`).\n\n4. **Hash quirk preserved**: The C `_hash` function has a bug (calls `EVP_DigestUpdate(msg)` twice when randomizer is non-NULL); my `compute_hash` mirrors this behavior to ensure compatibility.\n\n5. **Tests pass under the 60-second budget** in ~0.04 seconds runtime."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1052,"cache_read_input_tokens":96366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2ac4087-edf2-4d17-90f9-f8e9712356e5","uuid":"f45dc33e-1b4a-406d-bc02-bd4d6ec9912a"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1065377,"duration_api_ms":1029676,"ttft_ms":2161,"num_turns":57,"result":"All 3 tests pass. The implementation is working correctly:\n\n- `test_default` - Default context (SHA-384, default salt length)\n- `test_deterministic` - Deterministic blinding (SHA-384, salt_len=0)\n- `test_custom_parameters` - Custom context (SHA-256, salt_len=48)\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n1. **State management via side-channel maps**: The Rust types `BRSAContext`, `BRSAPublicKey`, `BRSASecretKey` have placeholder fields (`Option<EVP_PKEY>` etc.) that are opaque enums and can't store real data, so I use thread-safe `HashMap`s keyed by struct address to maintain the actual OpenSSL `Rsa` objects and context state.\n\n2. **PSS padding/verification implemented in pure Rust**: Custom `pss_encode`/`pss_verify` and `mgf1` functions because the openssl crate's high-level API doesn't expose `RSA_padding_add_PKCS1_PSS_mgf1` directly with custom modulus operations needed for blinding.\n\n3. **Blinding logic**: Uses `BigNum` arithmetic from the `openssl` crate (`mod_mul`, `mod_exp`, `mod_inverse`, `gcd`, `rand_range`).\n\n4. **Hash quirk preserved**: The C `_hash` function has a bug (calls `EVP_DigestUpdate(msg)` twice when randomizer is non-NULL); my `compute_hash` mirrors this behavior to ensure compatibility.\n\n5. **Tests pass under the 60-second budget** in ~0.04 seconds runtime.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b2ac4087-edf2-4d17-90f9-f8e9712356e5","total_cost_usd":4.43918225,"usage":{"input_tokens":61,"cache_creation_input_tokens":84273,"cache_read_input_tokens":3196092,"output_tokens":92565,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":84273},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7[1m]":{"inputTokens":61,